    "q-214179": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214179",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{7}=6$ and ${a}_{8}=-3.$ The common difference of this sequence is $d=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{7}$ from ${a}_{8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{8}-{a}_{7} \\\\  & =-3-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-9.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
