    "q-5274": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5274",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the common difference of an arithmetic sequence if its third and sixth terms are $2$ and $-22$, respectively.",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}=2,\\,{a}_{6}=-22.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=6$ and $m=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{6}-{a}_{3}}{6-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-22)-2}{6-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24}{3} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-8.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
