      "source_example_id": "e-14390",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Common Difference Given Two Non-Consecutive Terms",
      "kp_id": "e-14390"
    },
    "q-67317": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67317",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{20}=21.5$ and ${a}_{24}=12.5.$ What is the common difference of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *decreasing*, and therefore we expect $d$ to be *negative*.\n\nWe are given the terms\n\n$$\n{a}_{20}=21.5,\\,{a}_{24}=12.5.\n$$\n\nTo find $d,$ we apply the formula with $n=24$ and $m=20:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{n}-{a}_{m}}{n-m} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{24}-{a}_{20}}{24-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{12.5-21.5}{24-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{4} \\\\  & =-2.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=-2.25.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
